        <mxCell id="69" value="on miss" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="59" target="54"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>


        <mxCell id="99" value="" style="line;strokeWidth=3;html=1;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1320" width="2100" height="10" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="100" value="OPTIMAL REFERENCE (what a senior strong-hire would design)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1340" width="900" height="40" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="101" value="1. CORE ENTITIES" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1400" width="400" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="102" value="Post&#10;- postId: snowflake (time-sortable)&#10;- authorId&#10;- text&#10;- createdAt&#10;- lang, deleted: bool&#10;- version   (for reindex idempotency)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1435" width="320" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="103" value="IndexSegment  (a time bucket)&#10;- segmentId&#10;- timeRange: [from, to)&#10;- subShardCount: N&#10;- state: HOT | SEALED | COMPACTED | COLD&#10;- termFilter: bloom over distinct terms&#10;- docCount, sizeBytes" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="1435" width="400" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="104" value="PostingList  (inside a sub-shard)&#10;- term&#10;- docIds: postIds, DESC by createdAt&#10;  (delta-encoded, block-skippable)&#10;&#10;DELETED-ness lives in a tombstone bitset&#10;per segment, NOT in the posting list." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="820" y="1435" width="420" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="105" value="ENTITIES HE MISSED&#10;· IndexSegment as a first-class object — without it, bucket state,&#10;  subShardCount and the bloom filter have nowhere to live&#10;· deleted / tombstones — posts get deleted; the index must not serve them&#10;· version — makes reindexing idempotent over an at-least-once stream&#10;· lang — decides the tokenizer/analyzer per post" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1280" y="1435" width="840" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="110" value="2. API DESIGN" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1630" width="400" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="111" value="POST /v1/posts&#10;  Headers: Authorization: Bearer &lt;jwt&gt;  ·  Idempotency-Key: &lt;uuid&gt;   &lt;-- HE MISSED THIS&#10;  Body:     { text: string (max 300 chars), lang?: string }&#10;  201 -&gt;    { postId, createdAt }&#10;  Replaying the same Idempotency-Key returns the SAME postId, 200 not 201.&#10;  Rationale: write path is only 99.9% available (~9h/yr down) =&gt; clients WILL retry." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1665" width="1020" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="112" value="GET /v1/search&#10;  Query: q=world+cup  ·  limit=20 (default 20, max 100)  ·  cursor=&lt;opaque&gt;&#10;  200 -&gt; {&#10;          results: [ { postId, text, authorId, createdAt } ],&#10;          nextCursor: string | null,&#10;          searchedThrough: ISO8601        &lt;-- how far back the walk got&#10;        }&#10;  cursor encodes (createdAt, postId, segmentId) — a SNAPSHOT position, so&#10;  paging is stable: posts created after page 1 never appear on page 2.&#10;  searchedThrough lets the client say &quot;no more results before &lt;date&gt;&quot; honestly&#10;  instead of silently truncating a walkback that timed out." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="1665" width="1040" height="250" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="113" value="DELETE /v1/posts/{postId}   202 -&gt; { postId, status: &quot;DELETING&quot; }&#10;  Async: tombstone in Cassandra + a tombstone event on the same Kafka topic,&#10;  so the index removes it on the same ordered path as creates.&#10;Errors: 400 malformed query · 401 · 403 · 404 · 409 idempotency-key conflict&#10;        · 413 text too long · 429 rate limited (+ Retry-After) · 503 partial index unavailable" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1855" width="1020" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>


        <mxCell id="120" value="3. OPTIMAL HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2030" width="400" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="121" value="WRITE PATH" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#7F7F7F;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2070" width="300" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="122" value="Client" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2110" width="130" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="123" value="API Gateway&#10;auth · rate limit · routing" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="230" y="2100" width="180" height="80" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="124" value="Post Service&#10;idempotency-key dedup&#10;snowflake id assign" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="470" y="2100" width="190" height="80" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="125" value="Post Store&#10;Cassandra&#10;PK = postId&#10;source of truth" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="730" y="2060" width="180" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="126" value="Kafka  post-events&#10;key = postId&#10;create · delete · edit" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="730" y="2210" width="180" height="100" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="127" value="Indexer&#10;consumer group&#10;tokenize · analyze&#10;dedup on (postId, version)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="980" y="2205" width="200" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="128" value="DLQ&#10;poison messages" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1000" y="2360" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="130" value="SEARCH INDEX — segments by TIME, hot segment hash-subsharded" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#7F7F7F;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2070" width="700" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="131" value="HOT segment  (current hour)&#10;N = 32 sub-shards, hash(postId)&#10;takes ALL 30k/s peak writes&#10;near-real-time refresh ~1s" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFCCCC;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2105" width="270" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="132" value="SEALED segments  (recent days)&#10;compacted 32 -&gt; 4 sub-shards&#10;read-only, merged, optimized" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1560" y="2105" width="270" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="133" value="COLD segments  (years, ~20k)&#10;1 shard each, cheap storage&#10;reached only via bloom hit" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1870" y="2105" width="250" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="140" value="READ PATH" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#7F7F7F;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2470" width="300" height="24" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="144" value="Client" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2545" width="130" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="141" value="Search Coordinator&#10;· holds ALL segment bloom filters resident (~tens of GB)&#10;· skips a segment with a MEMORY lookup, never an RPC&#10;· walks newest -&gt; oldest, EARLY TERMINATES on a full page&#10;· deadline budget: stop at 400ms, return searchedThrough" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="230" y="2505" width="480" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="142" value="Query Result Cache&#10;Redis, key = (q, cursor)&#10;TTL ~30s&#10;absorbs head-query skew" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="770" y="2505" width="240" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="143" value="Hydration Cache&#10;Redis, key = postId&#10;500k-1M reads/s&#10;(NOT 100k — a page is 20 results)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1070" y="2505" width="270" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="150" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="122" target="123"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="151" value="POST /posts" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="123" target="124"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="152" value="write" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="124" target="125"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="153" value="emit event" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="124" target="126"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="154" value="consume" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="126" target="127"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="155" value="unparseable" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="127" target="128"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="156" value="index doc" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="127" target="131"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="157" value="seal + compact" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="131" target="132"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="158" value="age out" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="132" target="133"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="159" value="GET /search" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="144" target="141"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="160" value="check" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="141" target="142"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="161" value="postIds -&gt; posts" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="142" target="143"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="162" value="scatter to 1-2 segments only" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.15;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="141" target="131"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="163" value="on miss" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="143" target="125"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="170" value="4. KEY TRADE-OFFS  (choice vs NAMED alternative, and what it gives up)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2700" width="900" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="171" value="Time-bucketed segments  vs  hash-by-postId shards&#10;  Gives up: uniform write spread, and rare-term queries now need a walkback.&#10;  Buys: early termination — 1-2 segments per query instead of 20,000. Only legal&#10;  BECAUSE we committed to recency ordering; with BM25 relevance every segment&#10;  must be consulted and this whole design collapses. State that dependency out loud." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2735" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="172" value="Hash-subshard the HOT segment only  vs  subshard everything&#10;  Gives up: 32x fan-out and a p99 that is now the slowest of 32 responses.&#10;  Buys: 30k/s spread over 32 nodes. Compacting sealed segments back to ~4 confines&#10;  the tail-latency cost to one segment instead of all 20,000." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="2735" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="173" value="Cassandra for the post store  vs  sharded MySQL / DynamoDB&#10;  Gives up: no joins, no strong secondary indexes, tunable-consistency footguns.&#10;  Buys: 10k/s sustained append-only writes with linear scale-out and no resharding&#10;  ceremony. MySQL would need manual sharding at this write rate; Dynamo works but&#10;  costs materially more at 110 TB/year and never shrinks." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2905" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="174" value="Kafka between write and index  vs  dual-write from Post Service&#10;  Gives up: end-to-end latency, and search is now eventually consistent by construction.&#10;  Buys: the index can be down for an hour and lose nothing; replay rebuilds a corrupted&#10;  segment from the log. Dual-write means a crash between the two writes silently drops&#10;  a post from search forever, with nothing to detect it." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="2905" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="175" value="Bloom filters on the coordinator  vs  a global term -&gt; segment index&#10;  Gives up: false positives (wasted RPCs), tens of GB resident, and sync with the index.&#10;  Buys: skip decisions at memory speed. A global term index is exact but is itself a&#10;  distributed lookup on the hot path — you pay an RPC to avoid an RPC." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3075" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="176" value="Recency ordering  vs  relevance ranking (BM25 + engagement)&#10;  Gives up: result quality — the top result is the newest match, not the best one.&#10;  Buys: the entire early-termination design above. This is THE decision in this problem&#10;  and it must be stated as a scoping choice in requirements, not assumed silently." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="3075" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="180" value="5. DEEP DIVES" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3270" width="900" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="181" value="THE CORE BREAK — scatter-gather (he found this himself)&#10;300 GB/day index · 50 GB/shard -&gt; 6 shards/day -&gt; ~2,000/yr -&gt; ~20,000 after a few years.&#10;Every query touches every shard: 150k peak QPS x 20,000 = 3e9 shard-hits/s. Impossible.&#10;FIX: segment by time; recency ordering lets the coordinator stop as soon as a page is full,&#10;so a common-term query touches 1-2 segments." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3305" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="182" value="SECOND BREAK — write hotspot (he found this too)&#10;All 30k/s peak writes land on the newest segment; 20,000 older segments idle.&#10;FIX: hash-subshard the hot segment into N=32 by hash(postId) -&gt; ~1k/s each.&#10;Cost: p99 becomes the slowest of 32. Seal + compact to ~4 sub-shards once writes stop,&#10;so only the hot segment pays the fan-out tax." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="3305" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="183" value="THIRD BREAK — rare-term walkback (he found and fixed this)&#10;[&quot;zbigniew&quot;,&quot;kayak&quot;] forces a walk through 20,000 segments of empty posting lists.&#10;FIX: per-segment bloom filter of distinct terms, resident on the coordinator; skip is a&#10;memory lookup, not an RPC. Plus a HARD DEADLINE — stop at 400ms and return partial&#10;results with searchedThrough, rather than blowing the p99 SLA on a cold query." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3475" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="184" value="HOT KEYS — head-query skew (never raised)&#10;Search traffic is Zipfian: a breaking-news term can be 20%+ of all queries in a minute,&#10;and every one of those hits the same hot segment sub-shards.&#10;FIX: query-result cache keyed on (q, cursor) with a ~30s TTL in front of the coordinator,&#10;plus read replicas of the hot segment. A 30s-stale first page is invisible to users." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="3475" width="1030" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="185" value="CONSISTENCY &amp; CORRECTNESS (never raised)&#10;· Kafka is at-least-once =&gt; the SAME post can be indexed twice. Dedup on (postId, version)&#10;  at the indexer; indexing is then idempotent and replay is safe.&#10;· POST /posts needs an Idempotency-Key: the write path is 99.9% available (~9h/yr down),&#10;  so clients retry, so duplicate posts are a certainty, not a risk.&#10;· Deletes must flow down the SAME Kafka topic keyed by postId, so create and delete for one&#10;  post stay ordered. A deleted post served by search is a privacy incident, not a bug.&#10;· Cursor = (createdAt, postId, segmentId) snapshot position, so 10k posts/s arriving mid-&#10;  pagination cannot inject rows into page 2 or duplicate rows across pages." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3645" width="1030" height="210" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="186" value="OPERABILITY — the phase that never happened&#10;· FRESHNESS SLO first: &quot;a post is searchable within 5s, p99&quot;. Without it nothing below&#10;  has a threshold and &quot;broken&quot; has no definition.&#10;· Index lag metric: now - createdAt of the last indexed post, PER PARTITION (a global&#10;  average hides one stuck partition). Alert at &gt;30s.&#10;· Kafka consumer lag per partition; alert on sustained growth, not absolute value.&#10;· DLQ depth, with an alert on non-zero — a poison message silently stalls a partition.&#10;· Segment health: docCount vs expected, bloom-filter staleness, compaction backlog.&#10;· End-to-end canary: write a post with a known nonce token every 10s, search for it,&#10;  emit the observed delay. This is the ONLY check that tests the whole path.&#10;· Cost: 110 TB/yr forever =&gt; cold segments to cheap object storage with lazy hydration;&#10;  the time bucketing already gives you the tiering boundary for free.&#10;· Failure drill: indexer dies mid-batch -&gt; offsets uncommitted -&gt; replay -&gt; dedup makes it&#10;  a no-op. ES rejects a write -&gt; retry with backoff -&gt; DLQ -&gt; page on depth &gt; 0." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="3645" width="1030" height="290" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="187" value="CORRECTED TRAFFIC MODEL&#10;· 1B posts/day / 1e5 s = 10k posts/s avg · peak 3x = 30k/s · 9 MB/s at peak (not 3)&#10;· 300 GB/day = ~110 TB/year (not 90), retained forever&#10;· 5B searches/day = 50k/s avg · 150k/s peak&#10;· a page is ~20 results, so hydration is 1M reads/s at avg, 3M at peak — 10-30x the&#10;  100k he derived from &quot;2 posts per search&quot;. That number sizes the Redis tier." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFE6E6;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3875" width="1030" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
